<section class="section section--line" aria-labelledby="pain-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--split">
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__dot"></span>Common pain</span>
        <h2 id="pain-heading">Sound familiar?</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="reveal" style="--d:1">Most teams do not have a HubSpot problem. They have an architecture problem that shows up in HubSpot. The data was never structured, the pipeline was never designed around how deals actually close, and nobody documented how any of it works.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="bento" data-stagger>
      <article class="card card--feature">
        <div class="card-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-database" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
        <h3>Your data lives in four places and agrees in none of them</h3>
        <p>Duplicate contacts, half-filled fields, and exports into spreadsheets before anyone will believe a number.</p>
        <dl class="symptom"><dt>Symptom</dt><dd>30%+ duplicate rate</dd><dt>Fix</dt><dd class="fix">Golden record rules</dd></dl>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon card-icon--blue"><i class="fa-solid fa-diagram-project" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
        <h3>The pipeline does not match how deals actually close</h3>
        <p>Stages your reps skip, close dates nobody updates, and a forecast leadership quietly discounts.</p>
        <dl class="symptom"><dt>Symptom</dt><dd>Close-date drift</dd><dt>Fix</dt><dd class="fix">Exit-criteria gates</dd></dl>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon card-icon--cyan"><i class="fa-solid fa-hourglass-half" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
        <h3>Your team spends hours on work the CRM should do</h3>
        <p>Copy-pasting between tools, chasing status updates, and building lists by hand.</p>
        <dl class="symptom"><dt>Symptom</dt><dd>~8 hrs/rep lost</dd><dt>Fix</dt><dd class="fix">Automated routing</dd></dl>
      </article>
      <article class="card card--feature">
        <div class="card-icon card-icon--green"><i class="fa-solid fa-wand-magic-sparkles" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
        <h3>You are using a fraction of what you pay for</h3>
        <p>Licenses for Professional or Enterprise, running at the level of a basic contact database.</p>
        <dl class="symptom"><dt>Symptom</dt><dd>Tier shelfware</dd><dt>Fix</dt><dd class="fix">Portal architecture</dd></dl>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="what-we-do" aria-labelledby="what-heading">
  <div class="container split">
    <div class="split__sticky reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow__dot"></span>What we do</span>
      <h2 id="what-heading">Four things, done properly</h2>
      <p>We work on one platform. HubSpot architecture is the entire business, not a service line next to advertising and brand work. That focus is why we go deeper than a generalist agency will, and it is the reason clients bring us in after someone else has already had a go.</p>
      <p>We also build custom API integrations, run HubSpot audits, and provide ongoing administration and optimization for teams without an internal CRM owner.</p>
      <a href="/solutions/" class="btn btn-ghost">Explore our solutions <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i></a>
    </div>
    <div class="grid grid-2" data-stagger>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-cubes" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
        <h3>HubSpot implementation and onboarding</h3>
        <p>Set up the portal correctly the first time: objects, pipelines, lifecycle stages, permissions, automation, and reporting designed around your sales motion instead of HubSpot’s defaults.</p>
        <div class="card-meta"><span><b>Timeline</b> 2–4 wks</span><span><b class="is-blue">Includes</b> Schema + Permissions + Training</span></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon card-icon--blue"><i class="fa-solid fa-right-left" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
        <h3>CRM migration</h3>
        <p>Move from Salesforce, Pipedrive, or a legacy system with fields mapped, duplicates resolved, automation rebuilt, and history preserved where it matters. Your team lands in a working CRM, not a data dump.</p>
        <div class="card-meta"><span><b>Timeline</b> 3–6 wks</span><span><b class="is-blue">Includes</b> Field Map + Sandbox QA + Cutover</span></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon card-icon--cyan"><i class="fa-solid fa-broom" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
        <h3>CRM cleanup and data quality</h3>
        <p>Remove duplicate, incomplete, and conflicting records, then put validation rules and governance in place so the mess does not come back. Reporting and automation only work when the data underneath them is trustworthy.</p>
        <div class="card-meta"><span><b>Timeline</b> 1–2 wks</span><span><b class="is-blue">Includes</b> Audit + Deduplication + SOPs</span></div>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon card-icon--green"><i class="fa-solid fa-chart-line" aria-hidden="true"></i></div>
        <h3>RevOps infrastructure, lead to close</h3>
        <p>Connect the whole path: lifecycle stages, lead routing and SLAs, sales and marketing automation, attribution, and dashboards. Leadership sees the funnel, and qualified leads stop sitting unassigned.</p>
        <div class="card-meta"><span><b>Timeline</b> 2–4 wks</span><span><b class="is-blue">Includes</b> Full-Funnel KPIs + SLAs + Dashboards</span></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

